At the next station, a lot of people get in.
The U-Bahn is suddenly quite full.
An older man stops beside me.
"Excuse me, is this seat still free?" he asks.
"Yes, of course," I answer.
I move over a little bit.
That way he can sit comfortably.
The man sits down and smiles.
"Thank you very much," he says.
"The weather is really bad today."
"Yes, it is very gray and cold," I say.
"Unfortunately we have to wait for the summer," he says.
I laugh and nod.
"Are you traveling far with the U-Bahn?" he asks me then.
"Not very far," I answer.
"But I must soon change to the S-Bahn."
"I see," the man says.
"I am already getting out at the next station."
